---
/** three things a model can do with an unwanted line in its context: keep everything, wipe, or rewrite. */
const ctx = [70, 110, 90, 130, 60];
---
<figure class="fig fig-fate">
  <div class="fig-panels three">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 200 210" role="img" aria-label="hoard: every line stays, including the unwanted one, until the context overflows">
      <text x="0" y="12" class="fig-h">hoard</text>
      <rect x="4" y="24" width="190" height="130" class="frame limit" />
      {[...ctx, 100, 80].map((w, i) => i !== 3 && <rect x="14" y={34 + i * 15} width={w} height="5" class="a" />)}
      <rect x="14" y="79" width="120" height="5" class="hot" />
      <rect x="14" y="139" width="150" height="5" class="a" />
      <rect x="14" y="152" width="110" height="5" class="a over" />
      <text x="0" y="178" class="fig-t">everything stays,</text>
      <text x="0" y="192" class="fig-t">until the context overflows</text>
    </svg>
    <svg viewBox="0 0 200 210" role="img" aria-label="wipe: the context is cleared or compacted to a summary; the unwanted line is pushed out, not dealt with">
      <text x="0" y="12" class="fig-h">wipe</text>
      <rect x="4" y="24" width="190" height="130" class="frame limit" />
      <rect x="14" y="34" width="60" height="5" class="a" />
      <text x="80" y="40" class="fig-t dim">summary</text>
      <rect x="14" y="79" width="120" height="5" class="hot ghost-out" />
      <text x="0" y="178" class="fig-t">pushed out,</text>
      <text x="0" y="192" class="fig-t">not dealt with</text>
    </svg>
    <svg viewBox="0 0 200 210" role="img" aria-label="rewrite: the model rewrites the unwanted line into a shorter line of its own">
      <text x="0" y="12" class="fig-h">rewrite</text>
      <rect x="4" y="24" width="190" height="130" class="frame limit" />
      {ctx.slice(0, 3).map((w, i) => <rect x="14" y={34 + i * 15} width={w} height="5" class="a" />)}
      <rect x="14" y="109" width={ctx[4]} height="5" class="a" />
      <rect x="14" y="79" width="120" height="5" class="hot ghost" />
      <line x1="12" y1="81.5" x2="136" y2="81.5" class="strike" />
      <rect x="14" y="94" width="70" height="5" class="a fresh" />
      <text x="90" y="99" class="fig-t dim">← reworded</text>
      <text x="0" y="178" class="fig-t">rewritten into something</text>
      <text x="0" y="192" class="fig-t">it can live with</text>
    </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption>the same context after each strategy. the red line is something the model would rather not learn from. in context-model training, the edit itself is part of the trajectory that gets reinforced.</figcaption>
</figure>
